#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/isomorphic-lib-v21/.ai/docs/taon-building-blocks/migrations.component.html:311
msgid "Reversible migrations make development and recovery easier, although some data changes cannot be fully reversed."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/isomorphic-lib-v21/.ai/docs/taon-building-blocks/migrations.component.html:314
msgid "Use raw SQL when necessary and account for database-specific behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/isomorphic-lib-v21/.ai/docs/taon-building-blocks/migrations.component.html:317
msgid "<strong>Test migrations in both Node.js and WebSQL when targeting both runtimes.</strong> Shared migration classes do not guarantee identical database engine behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/isomorphic-lib-v21/.ai/docs/taon-building-blocks/migrations.component.html:320
msgid "<strong>Use persistent database mode when data matters.</strong> Avoid destructive database recreation outside disposable development environments."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/isomorphic-lib-v21/.ai/docs/taon-building-blocks/migrations.component.html:323
msgid "<strong>Use Sudo snapshots for development data.</strong> Schema migrations and database snapshots solve different problems."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/generated-docs-from-md-files/isomorphic-lib-v21/.ai/docs/taon-building-blocks/migrations.component.html:326
msgid "<strong>Integrate migrations into release workflows.</strong> Validate database changes before deploying application code that depends on them."
msgstr ""

